message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling about a hair clip craft kit. It is likely classified as a set under GRI 3(b) with the hair clips giving the set its essential character. Hair clips fall under heading 9615 (combs, hair-slides and the like). The relevant subheading is 9615.19 (other), with the statistical suffix 9615.19.6000 for "Other" (plastic hair clips). The alternative is 9615.11 (hard rubber or plastics combs, hair-slides), where 9615.11.3000 covers "Other" hair-slides. Claw clips are generally treated as hair-slides or barrettes under 9615.11, and the subheading for plastics is 9615.11.30 (valued over 20 cents each?).

HTSUS 9615.11: "Combs, hair-slides and the like: Of hard rubber or plastics": 9615.11.10 (combs, valued not over 4 cents?), 9615.11.20 (hair-slides, etc.), 9615.11.30 (other), 9615.11.3000 and 9615.11.5000... Having to commit, I recall 9615.11.3000 as "Other: Valued not over 20 cents each" and 9615.11.4000 as "Other." I also recall that in ruling NY N-type decisions, hair clips of plastics are classified in 9615.11.3000. I will go with 9615.11.3000.

{"hts_code": "9615.11.3000", "reason": "The kit is a GRI 3(b) set whose essential character comes from the plastic hair claw clips, which are classified as hair-slides and the like of plastics in heading 9615."}
